internal/engine/whatsmeow/session.go: Reuse an in-flight dial for pairing retries  # PR#6 — real, and a design rather than a guard: joining an existing dial means a shared result every caller can wait on, which is the same machinery M2 needs for idempotent sends. Building a one-off here would be a second one to retire. The retry meanwhile fails with ErrAlreadyConnected and the operator tries again, which is visible rather than silent.
# PR#6: real, and it needs the machinery M2 brings rather than a guard here. A second
# session pairing an account displaces the first mapping and deletes its device, but the
# displaced session's socket keeps working: WhatsApp allows several companion devices, so
# the new pairing does not unlink the old one, and only the next restart finds it
# unpaired. Ending it means reaching whichever instance runs it, which is a session-scoped
# stop over the fleet, the same thing the write fence above needs. Refusing the pairing
# instead is the other candidate and was not taken in M1: an operator whose old inbox was
# removed without a logout would have no way left to pair the number at all, and deciding
# that trade needs the Chatwoot side of the flow, not this package. The premise that made
# the deletion look safe ("WhatsApp has already unlinked them") was wrong and is corrected
# in the code comment.
internal/store/store.go: Reject pairings that displace a live session  # PR#6
